<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79826" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πάρπαρος:</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ᾧ ἀγὼν ἤγετο καὶ χοροὶ
		ἵσταντο</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i> (name of a mountain in Argolis) :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παρπαρώνια</span></b> , τά, festival held there, <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			5(1).213.44
		</span></i> (Sparta, V B.C.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παρπάρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>, ὁ, name of a
			place in Aeolis, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Fr.Hist.</u>
				7
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i> :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παρπαρώνιος</span></b> , ὁ, a citizen of
			it, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i> ; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παρπαριώτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.195.8
			</span></i>.</div>
